                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "da64d671-aed3-3bd7-b389-faf17656c3bf",
                        "entry_id": "f7e9a0b9-4015-3502-bf61-f9149d6012dc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative letter-case form of Latinize."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "nonstandard"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b3bab244-ed87-43d6-8c11-41cd861e2304",
                                "sense_id": "da64d671-aed3-3bd7-b389-faf17656c3bf",
                                "text": "But Theophrastus a Philoſopher ſo delicate, ſo modeft and ſo wife, was he not forced by reaſon, to dare to vtter this verſe, latinized by Cicero: / Vitam regit fortuna non ſapientia. / Fortune our life doth rule, / Not wiſedome of the ſchoole."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b37fd683-1016-43c3-becd-571ca1fb023c",
                                "sense_id": "da64d671-aed3-3bd7-b389-faf17656c3bf",
                                "text": "As a-curse is not found before the 12th c., the prefix does not here represent an older ar- or an-, but is imitated from the a- into which both of these had then sunk, and was apparently intensive, as in wake, a-wake, rise, a-rise. In 5, when the scribes latinized the Fr[ench] prefix a- before c to ac-, they servilely did the same with a-curse, whence the false spelling ac-curse."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
